prompt:
Write a creative story writing

- Primary goal: achieve early stakeholder alignment and reduce political execution risk for an industrial park mixed-use development.

- Key stakeholders to map and secure written buy-in from (three highest-impact parties): landowner; state ministry; anchor tenant.

- Commission targeted due diligence and financial assessments:
  - land due diligence;
  - environmental due diligence;
  - capex and opex estimates;
  - model a base-case IRR and downside scenario;
  - explicitly state any subsidies used in IRR assumptions.

- Develop procurement and investment-testing materials:
  - evaluate procurement approach options (competitive PPP vs negotiated concession);
  - prepare an outline term sheet to test investor appetite.

- Near-term milestones and timing (90-day diagnostic focus):
  - clarify land title;
  - secure commitment from one of three anchor tenants;
  - produce a draft financial model within 90 days.

- Risk management and public-value metrics:
  - define contingency triggers;
  - set a cost-per-job KPI to measure public value.

- Contextual facts and offers from the original message:
  - sender references having worked on a comparable mixed-use industrial scheme where early stakeholder alignment saved months on the timeline;
  - sender offers to help scope the 90-day diagnostic and introduce two private developers experienced in similar jurisdictions;
  - recipient named Chinedu; sender named Marcus.
